#>wonder_module_contract_overhaul_facet_operators
?["Which operator names each contract facet, and what do a concept edge <_foo and its { … } direction space mean at runtime?"]{
  #:depth #!semantic ~#lens(projection)
  ~#with: @plan @contract_spw @operator_detection @engagement
  ~#tension: "PLAN.md's facet table maps address, layer, substrate, wakes, probes, acts, binds, measure, ground, integrates and scene onto operators, and catalog/contract-spw.js already derives one sentence per module from it, marked as undecided. engagement-clusters waits on the same answer to prime clusters from Spw containers. One decision unblocks both; until then contracts stay flat fields and the sentence stays derived, never authored."
  ~#expect: "The derived sentence reads #>, #:, $, ~, ?, !, % and ( in that order. It has no @, = or . clause, because contract-spw.js derives only those eight facets and no def carries wakes or rests yet. Even the two defs with engages show no @, so the question is still open in the code."
  ~#probe(read)
  !probe{ "open /design/runtime/?spw-atlas=pulse-beat-tuner and read its contract as Spw against the facet table" }
  $%[contract.facets, operator.canon, engagement.clusters]
  ~<"./PLAN.md"> ~<"../engagement-clusters/PLAN.md">
}

